+## 2. Root cause (verified, not inferred)
+
+`tsc --noEmit` on the merge tree fails with exactly two errors:
+
+```
+src/tools/bridge.tools.ts(373,12): error TS2304: Cannot find name 'ClaimMarkerView'.
+src/tools/bridge.tools.ts(412,42): error TS2304: Cannot find name 'ClaimMarkerView'.
+```
+
+Mechanism: PR #3137 ("ROOT-CAUSE FIX (release-blind-spot): bridge.work.release writes an atomic-claim-release marker") relocates `ParsedClaimMarker` / `ClaimMarkerView` into the new `src/lib/claim_markers.ts` and keeps API compatibility in `src/tools/bridge.tools.ts` via:
+
+```ts
+export {
+  parseClaimMarkers, ATOMIC_CLAIM_RE, ATOMIC_CLAIM_RELEASE_RE, LEGACY_RELEASE_RE,
+} from "../lib/claim_markers.js";
+export type { ClaimMarkerView, ParsedClaimMarker } from "../lib/claim_markers.js";
+```
+
+A type-only **re**-export (`export type { X } from "…"`) publishes the name for downstream importers but does **not** create a binding in the exporting module's own scope. The two remaining local type annotations — `renewalDecision(markers: ClaimMarkerView, …)` (line 373) and `releaseDecision(markers: ClaimMarkerView, …)` (line 412) — therefore reference an unbound name. The value re-export (`export { parseClaimMarkers, … } from`) is unaffected, and `ParsedClaimMarker` is not referenced locally anywhere in the file, which is why tsc reports exactly these two errors and nothing else.
+
+## 3. The fix (2 lines) and its verification
+
+Extend the PR's existing import block in `src/tools/bridge.tools.ts`:
+
+```diff
+ import {
+   parseClaimMarkers,
++  type ClaimMarkerView,
+ } from "../lib/claim_markers.js";
+```
+
+That is the whole fix — the import statement (unlike the re-export) creates the local binding the two annotations need, and it is the binding the PR author already intended (the same lib module, same relative path).
